---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../seo/schema';

const origin = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://getaipractice.site');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site stores and what it never does: no accounts, no analytics, no third-party requests — progress and results stay in your browser alone."
  structuredData={[
    breadcrumbJsonLd(
      [
        { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
        { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' },
      ],
      origin,
    ),
  ]}
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">Privacy</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Short version: no accounts, no ads, no cross-site tracking. Everything you do here stays in your
    browser — the production deployment counts page views with cookieless, aggregate analytics, detailed
    below.
  </p>

  <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Progress</strong> — completed lessons, exercise attempts, XP and streak are stored in your
      browser's local storage under keys starting with <code>aip:</code>.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Assessment results</strong> — your last skills-check score is stored the same way.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Clearing your browser data clears all of it. Nothing is ever sent anywhere — there is no server
    component that receives personal data, because there are no accounts and no forms.
  </p>

  <h2>What the site does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No advertising and no third-party embeds.</li>
    <li>No cookies and no cross-site tracking.</li>
    <li>No email collection, no sign-ups, no profiles.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    The production deployment (on Vercel) uses Vercel Web Analytics: aggregate page-view and referrer
    counts, cookieless, with no way to identify or profile individual visitors. It loads only on the
    hosted deployment — local copies and non-Vercel builds of this site ship no analytics script at all.
    Counting page views was an explicit decision, recorded here first, as promised.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    Like every website, the host that serves these pages may keep short-lived standard server logs
    (IP address, time, requested page) for security and operations. That logging is infrastructure-level
    and identical on any site; this project does not read it, use it for profiling or share it.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections and contact</h2>
  <p>
    The site is in pre-launch build-out; a public correction channel opens with the launch and will be
    linked here. Until then, issues found during content audits are fixed in the lessons and recorded in
    the project's quality log.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this page</h2>
  <p>
    Analytics shipped on 2026-09-20 and is documented above. Any further feature that would collect or
    transmit data — ads, accounts, anything new — still requires a visible update to this page before it
    ships. The commitment stands: nothing extra without telling you here first.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
